A||||5||Ed||Chip failure||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||02-01-2000||09:29 PM||||On my way home tonight I saw an 87 GT parked with it's hoods up.  I went on over and found out the car had overheated.  <P>The driver said that he had just put in a performance chip, a brand you all know. He still had the box with the promise written on it that it, the chip, was programmed to keep the car from overheating. <BR>I gave the driver some handtools to use and he changed the chip back out.  <P>Well, what's going on here? Do the chips advance the timing and thereby make the engine run hotter?  And have any of you had the same problem?     ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||02-01-2000||10:11 PM||||i know when you buy those kits they come with different thermostats to make the car run cooler||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||02-02-2000||12:37 AM||||I asked him about changing the thermostat and he said the chip was supposed to keep the car from overheating.  <P>Maybe he missed something and should have changed the thermostat out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||02-02-2000||08:47 AM||||The chips that advertise anything to do with engine temp are usually supposed to be used with a thermostat and temp sensor made by the same vendor.  Chances are he didnt get the full story on the equipment before he installed it.  <P>Hope you mentioned the forum to him, wed get his problems straightened right up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||02-02-2000||01:57 PM||||Could be it ran hot because he was running the he!! out of it testing the chip??? Just a thought...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ed||02-02-2000||08:47 PM||||He did allow that he had been racing someone!||||reg||14
